<title>UK: Smith &amp; Nephew says FDA accepts application.</title>
<headline>Smith &amp; Nephew says FDA accepts application.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>British healthcare firm Smith &amp; Nephew Plc said on Wednesday the U.S. Food and Drug Administration had accepted a pre-market approval application (PMA) for its Dermagraft product to treat diabetic foot ulcers.</p>
<p>The application was being reviewed by the FDA under its expedited review process after its submission in December, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Smith &amp; Nephew formed a joint venture last year with U.S. firm Advanced Tissue Sciences Inc to commercialise Dermagraft.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
